{
  "id": "second-order-language",
  "term": "second-order language",
  "definition": "Second-order language refers to language understood as system-like patterns or constraints that shape how people engage in languaging. In this view, it is not separate from lived interaction but describes the broader regularities that guide whole-body, affective sense-making in social activity.",
