      "reasons": [
        "The definition blurs the packet’s distinction between first-order languaging and second-order language: the packet defines second-order language as “language as system like constraints,” while “whole-body, affective sense-making” is attributed to first-order languaging.",
        "The claim that second-order language is “not separate from lived interaction” is not stated that way in the packet and is stronger than the source supports.",
        "“Broader regularities that guide whole-body, affective sense-making in social activity” is an unsupported generalization beyond the packet’s wording about system-like constraints and behavior in interaction."
